          "new_text": "def filter_api_calls(\n    logp_with_result: np.ndarray,\n    logp_call_only: np.ndarray,\n    logp_no_call: np.ndarray,\n    tau_filter: float,\n) -> tuple[np.ndarray, np.ndarray]:\n    \"\"\"Return an ordered keep mask and one finite margin per proposed call.\"\"\"\n    # Validate threshold\n    if isinstance(tau_filter, bool):\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must not be a boolean\")\n    if not np.isfinite(tau_filter) or tau_filter < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"tau_filter must be a finite nonnegative number\")\n\n    # Validate inputs\n    arrays = [logp_with_result, logp_call_only, logp_no_call]\n    names = [\"logp_with_result\", \"logp_call_only\", \"logp_no_call\"]\n    for name, arr in zip(names, arrays):\n        if not isinstance(arr, np.ndarray):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a numpy array\")\n        if arr.ndim != 2:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be a 2-dimensional matrix\")\n        if arr.size == 0:\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must not be empty\")\n        if not np.all(np.isfinite(arr)):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} contains non-finite values\")\n        if np.any(arr > 0):\n            raise ValueError(f\"{name} must be nonpositive (all elements <= 0)\")\n\n    # Check shape match\n    if not (logp_with_result.shape == logp_call_only.shape == logp_no_call.shape):\n        raise ValueError(\"All input matrices must have the same shape\")\n\n    # Compute margins: sum over horizon (axis=1)\n    sum_with = np.sum(logp_with_result, axis=1)\n    sum_no = np.sum(logp_no_call, axis=1)\n    margins = sum_with - sum_no\n\n    # Keep mask: margins > tau_filter\n    keep_mask = margins > tau_filter\n\n    return keep_mask, margins"
